---
import Presentation from "../../../../components/Presentation.astro";
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";
import { Code as CodeSnippet } from "astro:components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Figure1 = `function addTax(price) {
  console.log(price * 1.08);
}

addTax(20);`;

const Figure2 = `function addTax(price) {
  return price * 1.08;
}

let total = addTax(20);
console.log(total);`;

const Figure3 = `function addTax(price) {
  return price * 1.08;
}

let cart = addTax(20) + addTax(35);
console.log(cart.toFixed(2));`;

const Figure4 = `function addTax(price) {
  return price * 1.08;
  console.log("Tax applied");
}`;

const Figure5 = `function addTax(price) {
  console.log(price * 1.08);
}

let total = addTax(20);
console.log(total);`;

const Task1 = `function addTax(price) {
  return price * 1.08;
}

let total = addTax(20);
console.log("Total:", total);
`;

const Task2 = `function addTax(price) {
  return price * 1.08;
}

function applyDiscount(price, percent) {
  return price - (price * percent / 100);
}

let discounted = applyDiscount(50, 20);
let final = addTax(discounted);

console.log("Discounted:", discounted.toFixed(2));
console.log("Final:", final.toFixed(2));
`;

const Task3 = `function addTax(price) {
  return price * 1.08;
}

function applyDiscount(price, percent) {
  return price - (price * percent / 100);
}

let final = addTax(applyDiscount(50, 20));
console.log("Final:", final.toFixed(2));

// Write a procedure called shippingFor that takes a weight
//   it returns 0 if the weight is under 1
//   it returns 5 if the weight is under 10
//   it returns 12 otherwise
// Print the shipping for 0.5, 4, and 20
`;

const ExampleOutput = `Final: 43.20
Shipping for 0.5: 0
Shipping for 4: 5
Shipping for 20: 12`;

const NotationJs = `function addTax(price) {
  return price * 1.08;
}

let total = addTax(20);`;

const NotationPseudo = `PROCEDURE addTax(price)
{
  RETURN(price * 1.08)
}

total ← addTax(20)`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Activity 2.3: Return Values</h1>
        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <!-- Launch / Concept -->
        <section id="launch">
          <Presentation>
            <section>
              <h2>Activity 2.3</h2>
              <h3 class="text-sn-theme">Return Values</h3>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Key Concepts</h2>
              <p>Printing vs. Handing Back</p>
              <p><code>return</code> Ends the Procedure</p>
              <p>Procedures Inside Procedures</p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>A Procedure That Only Prints</h2>
              <Code code={Figure1} frame="code" lang="javascript" title="No Return" showLineNumbers={false} />
              <p class="fragment">This works, once.</p>
              <p class="fragment">Now add up two taxed prices. You cannot &mdash; the number went to the screen and vanished.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Hand It Back Instead</h2>
              <Code code={Figure2} frame="code" lang="javascript" title="With Return" showLineNumbers={false} />
              <p class="fragment"><code>return</code> sends the value back to whoever called.</p>
              <p class="fragment">Now it is a value you can store, print, or use again.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Which Is Which</h2>
              <p><b>Printing</b> puts something on the screen. The program cannot use it.</p>
              <p class="fragment"><b>Returning</b> hands a value back. The screen sees nothing.</p>
              <p class="fragment">A procedure can do both. Most should do one.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Now It Composes</h2>
              <Code code={Figure3} frame="code" lang="javascript" title="Two Calls in One Expression" showLineNumbers={false} />
              <p class="fragment">Each call becomes its value, then the arithmetic happens.</p>
              <p class="fragment">You could not do this with a printing procedure.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Return Ends It</h2>
              <Code code={Figure4} frame="code" lang="javascript" title="Unreachable Code" showLineNumbers={false} />
              <p class="fragment">The <code>console.log</code> never runs.</p>
              <p class="fragment"><code>return</code> does not just set a value &mdash; it <b>leaves the procedure immediately</b>.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>The Silent One</h2>
              <Code code={Figure5} frame="code" lang="javascript" title="No Return, But Stored Anyway" showLineNumbers={false} />
              <p class="fragment"><code>total</code> is <code>undefined</code>.</p>
              <p class="fragment">No error. The procedure printed something and handed back nothing.</p>
              <p class="fragment">This is the most common return bug there is.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Today's Objectives</h2>
              <ul>
                <li>Writing a procedure that returns a value</li>
                <li>Explaining the difference between printing and returning</li>
                <li>Using a returned value in an expression or another call</li>
                <li>Recognizing why a procedure with no <code>return</code> gives <code>undefined</code></li>
              </ul>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Key Terms</h2>
              <div class="text-start">
                <dl>
                  <dt>Return value</dt>
                  <dd>The value a procedure hands back to its caller.</dd>
                  <dt>return</dt>
                  <dd>Sends a value back <i>and</i> exits the procedure immediately.</dd>
                  <dt>undefined</dt>
                  <dd>What a procedure hands back when it has no <code>return</code>.</dd>
                  <dt>Composition</dt>
                  <dd>Using one procedure's return value as another's argument.</dd>
                </dl>
              </div>
            </section>

          </Presentation>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Build -->
        <section id="build">
          <h2>Build</h2>

          <p>
            Create a new <b>JavaScript program</b> named{" "}
            <b class="text-sn-theme">2-3-return</b>.
          </p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Task 1: Return Instead of Print</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Write the code below and run it.</li>
            <li>Change <code>return</code> to <code>console.log</code> and run it again.</li>
            <li><b>Write down what changed.</b> One of the two prints <code>undefined</code>.</li>
          </ul>
          <Code code={Task1} frame="code" lang="javascript" title="Return Values" class="mt-3" />

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Task 2: Two Procedures, One Chain</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Add <code>applyDiscount</code> and run it.</li>
            <li>Check the arithmetic by hand: 20% off 50, then 8% tax.</li>
          </ul>
          <Code code={Task2} frame="code" lang="javascript" title="Return Values" class="mt-3" />

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Task 3: Compose Them Directly</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Note the nested call on the first line. Run it and confirm it matches Task 2.</li>
            <li>Then fill in the comment block.</li>
          </ul>
          <Code code={Task3} frame="code" lang="javascript" title="Return Values" class="mt-3" />

          <h5 class="mt-4">Challenge (optional)</h5>
          <ul>
            <li>Add <code>console.log("done")</code> immediately after a <code>return</code> line. Run it. Explain why nothing prints, and what that tells you about <code>return</code>.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Exam Notation -->
        <section id="exam-notation">
          <h2>Same Idea, Exam Notation</h2>

          <div class="row g-3 my-4">
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <Code
                code={NotationJs}
                frame="code"
                lang="javascript"
                title="JavaScript"
                showLineNumbers={false}
              />
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <Code
                code={NotationPseudo}
                frame="code"
                lang="txt"
                title="Exam Notation"
                showLineNumbers={false}
              />
            </div>
          </div>

          <p>Two differences, and one of them is easy to miss:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><code>RETURN</code> is capitalized and <b>takes parentheses</b> &mdash; <code>RETURN(expression)</code>, not <code>RETURN expression</code>.</li>
            <li>Assignment is <code>&larr;</code>, so capturing the result is <code>total &larr; addTax(20)</code>.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            The reference sheet says a <code>RETURN</code> may appear anywhere in the
            body and causes an immediate return &mdash; the same behavior you saw in
            the unreachable-code slide.
          </p>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Checkpoint -->
        <section id="checkpoint">
          <h2>Checkpoint</h2>

          <p>Your program should produce output like this.</p>

          <Code
            code={ExampleOutput}
            frame="terminal"
            lang="txt"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            title="Example Output"
          />

          <p class="mt-3">The 43.20 comes from 20% off 50, then 8% tax. Check it by hand before you trust it.</p>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Reflection -->
        <section id="reflection">
          <h2>Reflection</h2>

          <p>Answer these before submitting your work.</p>

          <ol>
            <li>A procedure prints a value instead of returning it. Name one thing you can no longer do with that value.</li>
            <li>Why does storing the result of a printing procedure give <code>undefined</code> rather than an error?</li>
            <li>Written response 2(b) on the exam asks you to describe a change that causes a run-time error. Describe one you could make to <code>shippingFor</code>.</li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Submit -->
        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>Submit the required files to the appropriate dropbox.</p>

          <h1
            class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash"
          >
            Activity Complete
          </h1>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
